@startuml assessment-service-class-diagram
title Level 3: Code - Class Diagram (assessment-service) - FR-04\nOwner: Ahmed Mohamed Ahmed
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
  BackgroundColor<<component>> #D5EFE0
  BorderColor<<component>> #2E8B57
}
skinparam interface {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide empty members

legend right
  |<#D5EFE0>   | Class of a component |
  |<#FFFFFF>   | Interface / domain class |
  | Solid arrow, open head | Uses (required interface / class) |
  | Dotted arrow, hollow head | Implements (provided interface) |
  | Filled diamond | Composition |
  | Plain line | Association |
endlegend

interface IAssessment <<provided>> {
  +addAssignment(data): Assignment
  +addExam(data): Exam
  +setStatus(assignmentId, status): void
  +setExamReminder(examId, daysBefore): void
  +getDeadlines(studentId, days): List<Deadline>
}

class AssessmentService <<component>> {
  -repository: IAssignmentRepository
  -assessmentValidator: AssessmentValidator
  --
  +addAssignment(...) / addExam(...)
  +setStatus(...) / setExamReminder(...)
  +getDeadlines(...)
}

IAssessment <|.. AssessmentService
class AssessmentValidator <<component>> {
  +validate(data): ValidationResult
}
AssessmentService --> AssessmentValidator

interface IAssignmentRepository <<required - Database>> {
  +save(item: Assignment): void
  +findById(id): Assignment
  +findByOwner(ownerId): List<Assignment>
}

AssessmentService --> IAssignmentRepository
class Assignment {
  -assignmentId: String
  -courseId: String
  -title: String
  -dueDate: Date
  -priority: String
  -status: String
  --
  +isOverdue(): boolean
}
class Exam {
  -examId: String
  -courseId: String
  -title: String
  -date: Date
  -time: Time
  -location: String
  -reminderDays: int
}
class Deadline {
  -itemId: String
  -title: String
  -due: Date
  -type: String
}
IAssignmentRepository --> Assignment
Assignment ..> Deadline
Exam ..> Deadline
note bottom of AssessmentService
SOLID applied:
S - AssessmentService only coordinates; AssessmentValidator each do one job.
O - new behaviour is added by new implementations, not by editing AssessmentService.
L - AssessmentService can replace any other IAssessment implementation.
I - IAssessment has only the operations its clients use.
D - AssessmentService depends on interfaces (IAssignmentRepository), not on concrete classes.
end note
@enduml
